## Key Definitions

| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| **Design Pattern** | How code is organised **within a single project** (e.g. MVC) |
| **Architecture** | How **multiple systems and services** are organised together |
| **System Design** | The process of designing end-to-end solutions to complex problems, resulting in an architecture |

---

## Design Patterns — MVC

MVC (Model-View-Controller) splits a codebase into three logical responsibilities:

| Layer | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| **Model** | Represents data, handles all database communication |
| **View** | Manages what the user sees (HTML/CSS rendering) |
| **Controller** | Coordinates between Model and View based on user requests |


> 💡 MVC is a **code organisation pattern** — all three layers can live on a single server. It does not imply physical separation.

