## Three-Tier Architecture

Three-tier architecture physically separates the system into three distinct services, each on its own server:

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[👤 User] -->|HTTP Request| B

    subgraph Presentation Tier
        B[Frontend\nReact / JavaScript]
    end

    B -->|API Call| C

    subgraph Application Tier
        C[Backend\nDjango / Python]
    end

    C -->|Query| D

    subgraph Data Tier
        D[Database\nPostgreSQL]
    end
```

### Example Technology Stack

| Tier | Technology | AWS Hosting |
|---|---|---|
| **Frontend** | React / JavaScript | S3 |
| **Backend** | Django / Python | EC2 |
| **Database** | PostgreSQL | RDS |

> ⚠️ Moving to three-tier requires config changes — the frontend now makes HTTP requests to the backend, and the backend uses a network connection string to reach the DB.

